$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$
Param1 =        	$ Autobaud
0,          		$ reserved
6,          		$ Link Path Size
"20 0f 24 01 30 01", 	$ Link Path to disable autobaud attribute.
0x0002,         	$ No support for settable path, scaling, scaling links, or
					$ real time update of value.  Value is gettable and 
					$ Settable.  Enumerated strings are supported.
4,          		$ Data Type - boolean
1,          		$ Data Size
"Autobaud",     	$ Parameter Name
"",         		$ Units String
			$$$$$$$$$$ Help string $$$$$$$$$$$
"Setting this parameter ON disables the Autobaud feature in the block. The change occures after the next power up. The default is Enabled.",
0,1,0,          	$ Min, Max, and Default values
1,1,1,0,0,0,0,0,0;      $ Not Used

$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$
Param2 =        	$ Output Fault State (group)
0,          		$ reserved
6,          		$ Link Path Size
"20 0F 24 03 30 01", 	$ Link Path to DOG status attribute.
0x0002,         	$ No support for settable path, scaling, or scaling links.
			$ Value is gettable and settable. Enumerated strings are supported.
24,         		$ Data Type - 8 bit string
1,          		$ Data Size - (in bytes)
"Output Fault State",   $ Parameter Name
"",         		$ Units String
			$$$$$$$$$$ Help string $$$$$$$$$$$
"Checking these boxes causes the outputs to Hold Last State during a communications fault. Leaving them blank lets the Output Fault Value parameter determine whether the outputs should be forced ON or OFF during a communications fault.",
0,255,0,         	$ Min, Max (max enumeration #), and Default values
1,1,1,0,0,0,0,0,0;  $ Not Used

